<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Ulster Bank names Wilson as chief exec designate.</title>
<headline>Ulster Bank names Wilson as chief exec designate.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ulster Bank, the Irish subsidiary of National Westminster Bank Plc, said on Thursday that it had appointed Martin Wilson as deputy group chief executive with effect from March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>Wilson will assume the role of chief executive of Ulster Bank when the current CEO, Ronnie Kells, retires in 1998.</p>
</text>
